 "notes": "Second read 2026-10-27: Southern Maine Middle School Relays (printed 'Souther Maine Middle School Relays', September 20, 2006, hosted by Traip Academy at Fort Foster); school names written '<town> Middle School' ('Messabesec' is Massabesic). Races 1-5 (one runner per school per heat) match the parse row for row; Open Race: the parse kept only the 10 rows whose time carries a minute; the other 39 are printed as bare seconds with the minute lost. The minute is recovered from the place order (each bare number is seconds after the last printed minute, rolling to the next minute when the seconds fall), e.g. 4 Snow 12:32 after 12:05, 12 Danici 13:10 after 13:05, 23 Murray 14:07 ('7') after 14:02, 37 Zotos 15:42 after 15:09; every inferred time lies between the printed full times around it (11:28 < 11:57 < 12:05 < ... < 13:05 < ... < 14:02 < ... < 15:09 < ... < 16:18 < ... < 17:04 < ... < 19:03 < 19:35). All 49 open-race rows are written. Races 2 and 3 have rows with no mark that are left out: race 2 places 4 N. Smith (Massabesic), 5 C. Fitzgerald (York), 8 Curti (Shapleigh); race 3 places 3 Strout (Saco), 6 M. Sutryn (Wells)."
